===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|dated}} A building containing a [[bar]] licensed to sell [[alcoholic]] [[drink]]s, and offering sleeping [[accommodation]]s for travelers.
#: {{syn|en|inn|Thesaurus:pub}}
#* {{RQ:Lyly Mother Bombie|act=II|scene=ii|page=28|passage=I maruell I heare no nevves of ''Dromio'', either hee ſlackes the matter, or betraies his Maiſter, I dare not motion anie thing to ''Stellio'', till I knovv vvhat my boy hath don, Ile hunt him out, if the loiterſacke be gone ſpringing into a '''Tauerne''', Ile fetch him reeling out.}}
#* {{RQ:Khayyam FitzGerald Rubaiyat|page=1|passage=Dreaming when Dawn's Left Hand was in the Sky / I heard a Voice within the '''Tavern''' cry, / "Awake, my Little ones, and fill the Cup / Before Life's Liquor in its Cup be dry."}}
#* {{RQ:Besant Ivory Gate|chapter=The Select Circle|page=46|passage=At half-past nine on this Saturday evening the parlor of the Salutation Inn, High Holborn, contained most of its customary visitors. {{...}} In former days every '''tavern''' of repute kept such a room for the select circle—a club, or society, of ''habitués'', who met every evening for a pipe and a cheerful glass.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:William Irwin Thompson|title=The Time Falling Bodies Take to Light: Mythology, Sexuality and the Origins of Culture|location=London|publisher=Rider/Hutchinson & Co.|year=1981|page=201|passage=At one of the way-stations on his long journey a barmaid at a '''tavern''' speaks to Gilgamesh and tries to give him common sense on the human condition.}}
# A [[restaurant]] or [[bar]].

